==English==
Likely akin to M.Du., M.L.G., E.Fris. ''tateren'' - "to chatter, babble", possibly of imitative origin. Attested in 1481, in William Caxton's translation of "[[w:Reynard|The History of Reynard the Fox]]".
===Verb===
{{en-verb|tattles|tattling|tattled|tattled}}

# {{intransitive|pejorative}} To [[report]] others' [[wrongdoing]]s or [[violations]]; to [[tell on]] somebody; to [[gossip]] or to disclose [[incriminating]] information.
# {{intransitive}} To [[chatter]].

====Synonyms====
* [[blow the whistle]]
* [[gossip]]

